        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "mortals the dice-pieces ( शार Marâthi सोंगट्या, ) and day and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "night the two dice. S'iva may also be regarded as the Destroyer",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "as he is described in the Puráṇas as playing at dice with his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "wife, Pàrvatî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 44. व्यापारैः—avocations, affairs. गुरु–momentous, weighty.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "कालः—Time, i. e. the passing away of time. त्रासः—fear or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "disgust. जन्म &c.—a comp. of the समाहारद्वंद्व class. मोहमयीं—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "मोहप्रचुरां the aff. मय is used in the sense of ‘excess’ ( or made",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of ). मदिरा—derived from मद् + किरच् ( इर ) + टाप् ( आ )—that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "which intoxicates. उन्मत्तभूतम्—उन्मत्तं भूतं; there is no special",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "propriety of taking भूत in the sense of इव. The poet makes a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "definite assertion here.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 45. निभृतम्—resolutely, steadily, or secretly. पुनरुक्त—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "i. e. repeatedly enjoyed, hence stale कदर्धिताः—disgraced; or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tormented. See Nit. s 84; and Infra, कदशनम् Mis Sl. 29.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 46. संसारविच्छित्ति—Cutting asunder, or utter destruction,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of the bonds of संसार, leading to moksha ( salvation or unification",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "with the Supreme Being). This is attained by means of Yoga",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "and then there is no re-birth for man. This is the highest",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ideal; the next one is स्वर्ग, This is attained by means of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "religious merit, vows, sacrifices &c ; see com. The reward for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "these is स्वर्ग, and after the heavenly happiness is enjoyed for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "the prescribed term, there is again rebirth, again the acquisition",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "of स्वर्ग by religious merit, again re-birth, and so on till the end",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "of the creation. धर्मः—see com. The student can easily see the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "difference between संसारविच्छित्ति and स्वर्गप्राप्ति. In the eyes of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "a philosophes, the latter is nothing ( तुच्छ ) as compared to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "former. रामा०—This refers to the third object of human",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "pursuit, viz. काम or the enjoyment of worldly pleasures. यौवनवन",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "—Not a happy metaphor, as वन expresses a plurality of ideas.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "It is probably used for alliteration. Or the poet may seem",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "to refer by Vana to an avenue of trees which gradually disap-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "pears as tree after tree is cut down and so to refer to the gradual",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "disappearance of youth. वयम्—The plural is used to indicate",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "self-disparagement.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
